# 
# 
<http://llod.jerteh.rs/alo/alo.owl#HateSpeech> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Any communication that disparages a person or a group on the basis of some characteristic such as race, color, ethnicity, gender, sexual orientation, nationality, religion, or other characteristics (Basile et al., 2019)."@en .
<http://llod.jerteh.rs/alo/alo.owl#HateSpeech> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "HateSpeech"@en .
# 
<http://llod.jerteh.rs/alo/alo.owl#Profanity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Profanity: This term encompasses a broader range of offensive language, including swearing, cursing, and other vulgar expressions. Profanity generally refers to language that is disrespectful or irreverent, especially towards sacred thing (Wikipedia)"@en .
<http://llod.jerteh.rs/alo/alo.owl#Profanity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Untargeted offensive language that is considered socially offensive due to being vulgar, obscene, or irreverent (Caselli et al., 2020, Britanicca)."@en .
<http://llod.jerteh.rs/alo/alo.owl#Profanity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Profanity"@en .
# 
<http://llod.jerteh.rs/alo/alo.owl#SexualOrientation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Represents sexual orientation as the characteristic on the basis of which an individual or group is targeted by abusive speech."@en .
<http://llod.jerteh.rs/alo/alo.owl#SexualOrientation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SexualOrientation"@en .
